      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Please add a unit test covering the `command_ble_hci_adv` bounds checks.\n\n### Review Summary\n\n* **Functionality:** ✅ Replacing `\u003e sizeof(...)` with `\u003e\u003d ARRAY_SIZE(...)` for `adverts`, `adv_params`, and `scans` in `command_ble_hci_adv()` properly restricts `adv`, `p`, and `scan_rsp` to valid element indices (`[0, 1]`).\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ Input bounds validation is co-located at the point where console arguments are parsed in `command_ble_hci_adv()` and follows standard ChromiumOS EC console command conventions.\n* **Code Simplicity:** ✅ The fix is minimal and direct, changing only the three bounds comparisons without introducing unnecessary state or control flow.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ✅ Using `ARRAY_SIZE(...)` instead of `sizeof(...)` on pointer arrays is the idiomatic ChromiumOS EC construct and avoids hardcoded array bounds.\n* **Security:** ✅ Prevents out-of-bounds pointer reads from `adverts`, `adv_params`, `scans`, `adv_lengths`, and `scan_lengths` when handling `ble_hci_adv` console arguments.\n* **Testing:** ❌ Missing automated unit test coverage for `command_ble_hci_adv()` boundary conditions (`0`, `1`, `-1`, `2`, `3`, and non-numeric inputs for `adv`, `p`, and `scan_rsp`); see inline comment on `common/btle_hci_controller.c`.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ✅ `Size: XS (+3, -3)`. Single, cohesive logical change fixing the array bounds checks in `command_ble_hci_adv()`.\n* **Commit Message:** ✅ Concise and accurate explanation of the problem and fix, with proper ChromiumOS `BUG\u003d` and `TEST\u003d` tags. [🔗](http://go/tj/8c3caada-9a16-414b-975a-f42ec5be2044)",
